            source: "Finance Act 1920 (income tax and super-tax); Trade Disputes Act 1906; Factory and Workshop Act 1901 (no general eight-hour law); Old Age Pensions Act 1908, National Insurance Act 1911 (health and unemployment), Unemployment Insurance Act 1920; Education Act 1918 (school to 14); Representation of the People Act 1918 (all men at 21, women at 30 with property); Church of England established (Welsh Church Act 1914, in force 1920); Aliens Restriction (Amendment) Act 1919 and Aliens Order 1920; British Broadcasting Company licence and receiving fee 1922; Military Service Acts lapsed 1920; free trade kept apart from the McKenna and Safeguarding duties; colonies: indirect rule (Lugard, Nigeria 1914) and hut and poll taxes",
        ),
